{"name":"Dolphin at Play","hex":"#b7b8bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dolphin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A carnivorous cetacean, typically with a beak-like snout, famed for their intelligence and occasional willingness to approach humans.","Tursiops truncatus, (Atlantic bottlenose dolphin) the most well-known species."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A man-made semi submerged maritime structure, usually installed to provide a fixed structure for temporary mooring, to prevent ships from drifting to shallow water or to serve as base for navigational aids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dolphin"},{"term":"play","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act in a manner such that one has fun; to engage in activities expressly for the purpose of recreation or entertainment.","To toy or trifle; to act with levity or thoughtlessness; to be careless."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Activity for amusement only, especially among the young.","Similar activity in young animals, as they explore their environment and learn new skills."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/play"}],"entries":[{"title":"At Play","blocks":[{"text":"At Play is a compilation album by Canadian electronic music producer Deadmau5. It is the first installment of Play Records' At Play series. It was released on October 20, 2008."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/At_Play_%28cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/At_Play","wikidata":"Q1953264"},{"title":"Dolphin","blocks":[{"text":"A dolphin is any one of the 40 extant species of aquatic mammal from the cetacean families Delphinidae, Platanistidae, Iniidae, Pontoporiidae, and the probably extinct Lipotidae. All these families belong to the parvorder Odontoceti, i.e., toothed whales, which also include the closely related families Monodontidae and Phocoenidae (porpoises), as well as the more distant families Physeteroidea and Ziphiidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Tursiops_truncatus_01.jpg/330px-Tursiops_truncatus_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin","wikidata":"Q7369"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Deadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg/250px-Deadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Deadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Deadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg/250px-Deadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeadmau5-At_Play_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Delfinekko.gif/330px-Delfinekko.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Delfinekko.gif/330px-Delfinekko.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Biosonar by cetaceans","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADelfinekko.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg/500px-Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg/1280px-Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg/500px-Dolphin_Encounter-9563.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu